	(text "Pin 1 = OUTx, pin 2 = that load's ground return (DEC-013 rev. B: AT13-2P-BM04, 5.40 mm pitch).\nLAYOUT: each pin 2 return carries up to 10 A, like its OUTx: same copper and via treatment.\n  Route pin 2 returns to the power-entry ground star region, never across the logic ground.\n  Up to 60 A of load return flows from the headers to the star region and out through J902.\nRELEASE-BLOCKING: verify which cavity is pin 1 on a sample (swap = OUTx on the ground wire)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 355.6 0)
		(effects
