	(text "CONNECTORS (Node60 harness page; REQ-NET-001: four node conductors: T1S pair, battery, ground; optional pass-through)\nMating sets (plugs, sockets, seals, wire sizes, keys) are harness parts, frozen together (harness page).\nJ901/J910 battery and J902/J911 return: Würth REDCUBE 74660016R M6 terminals with SurLok Plus receptacles,\n  busbar-joined in the case; the second pair passes battery and ground to a downstream node (DEC-016).\n  Fuse at the source sized for both nodes; the downstream node needs its own protection.\n  J901/J902 copper: 60 A plus the downstream current (see p2 note); J904-J909 pins 1 and 2: 10 A each (see p6 note).\n  Fuse: primary fuse at the battery/source end (off-board); per-feed fuses if dual-fed.\nJ903 T1S: Amphenol Sine ATM13-2P-BM04 (DEC-014), sealed two-way. ESD (D501/D502) right behind it (DEC-012).\nJ904-J909 outputs: Amphenol Sine AT13-2P-BM04 right-angle headers, one per output (DEC-013 rev. B; replaced\n  the TE DT13-2P), 10 A per output, 14 AWG minimum; validate contact derating at +125 C.\n  Pin 2 is the load's ground return: J902 now carries the whole node return (up to 60 A of load current).\nNo KL15, ignition or local wake input (DEC-007).\nUNVERIFIED (release-blocking): every connector mate, pinout and current rating.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.5 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "21d611b3-b87a-549e-9cd6-72260cdd441f")
	)
